            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a2-a10">

                <pb facs="0369" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg359"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 10 in No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Graham to Sir P.
                        Wodehouse.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate, Cape
                                Town,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 5, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The confederate steamer Alabama has just
                    captured an American bark off Green Point, or about four miles from the nearest
                    land (Robben island.) I witnessed the capture with my own eyes, as did hundreds
                    of others at the same time. This occurrence at the entrance of Table bay, and
                    clearly in British waters, is an insult to England, and a grievous injury to a
                    friendly power, the United States.</p>
                <p>Towards the government of my country and her domestic enemies the government of
                    England assumes a position of neutrality, and if the neutrality can be infringed
                    with impunity in this bold and daring manner, the government of the United
                    States will no doubt consider the matter as one requiring immediate
                    explanation.</p>
                <p>Believing that the occurrence was without your knowledge or expectation, and
                    hoping you will take such steps to redress the outrage as the exigency
                    requires,</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WALTER GRAHAM, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
